1
00:00:09,693 --> 00:00:11,987
You should go in.
I'll see you at the office.

2
00:00:17,159 --> 00:00:18,369
Mr. Dokgo.

3
00:00:29,922 --> 00:00:32,633
Would you like to go
on a date with me?

4
00:00:33,592 --> 00:00:34,593
A date?

5
00:00:36,971 --> 00:00:39,890
Are you attracted to me
by any chance?

6
00:00:42,685 --> 00:00:43,811
Goodness.

7
00:00:44,979 --> 00:00:47,231
Yes, a bit.

8
00:00:47,314 --> 00:00:48,399
So

9
00:00:50,109 --> 00:00:51,193
you want to sleep with me?

10
00:00:54,822 --> 00:00:55,823
What?

11
00:00:58,367 --> 00:01:02,621
No, that's not what I meant.

12
00:01:02,705 --> 00:01:04,790
That's what a date means to me.

13
00:01:04,873 --> 00:01:08,127
We can grab a meal,
have coffee, and go for a walk.

14
00:01:08,210 --> 00:01:10,337
That's my idea of a date.

15
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:13,924
Isn't that what we do every day
at work?

16
00:01:15,009 --> 00:01:16,302
Anyway, too bad.

17
00:01:17,011 --> 00:01:19,054
I don't date my coworkers.

18
00:01:20,639 --> 00:01:24,560
Well, if you still find me attractive
after the contract ends

19
00:01:24,643 --> 00:01:26,145
talk to me again.

20
00:01:29,732 --> 00:01:30,858
Good night.

21
00:01:42,911 --> 00:01:44,913
- Hello?
- <i>Dal, where are you?</i>

22
00:01:44,997 --> 00:01:46,749
<i>It's a hit.</i>
<i>Check our website right now.</i>

23
00:01:46,832 --> 00:01:47,875
<i>It's insane.</i>

24
00:01:47,958 --> 00:01:50,210
<i>Ms. Gong, this is incredible.</i>

25
00:01:53,797 --> 00:01:56,175
I was scared the server would go down
on the weekend.

26
00:01:56,592 --> 00:01:58,677
Look how the views have skyrocketed.
Isn't that crazy?

27
00:02:00,095 --> 00:02:01,555
Is that real-time?

28
00:02:01,639 --> 00:02:03,474
Yes, we're getting endless reviews.

29
00:02:03,807 --> 00:02:06,268
There are many people
visiting the stores in person.

30
00:02:06,727 --> 00:02:08,187
Should we get ready?

31
00:02:08,896 --> 00:02:11,982
How is that possible
in such a short time?

32
00:02:12,066 --> 00:02:14,401
Some influencer said
it was a gift from her boyfriend

33
00:02:14,485 --> 00:02:15,986
during her livestream.

34
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:18,656
She said
the candle especially was impressive.

35
00:02:18,739 --> 00:02:21,450
Right. It actually works quite well
to set the mood.

36
00:02:23,202 --> 00:02:24,203
Everyone.

37
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:27,039
I have more good news.

38
00:02:27,706 --> 00:02:30,292
I got a call from JC Investments.

39
00:02:31,085 --> 00:02:34,296
They want to meet Mr. Dokgo!

40
00:03:44,783 --> 00:03:45,868
About the other day

41
00:03:46,994 --> 00:03:49,788
I just felt grateful.

42
00:03:50,456 --> 00:03:52,666
So I wanted to treat you

43
00:03:53,041 --> 00:03:54,460
to a meal or something.

44
00:03:54,543 --> 00:03:56,754
Besides

45
00:03:56,837 --> 00:03:58,714
I'm easily drawn to everything.

46
00:03:58,797 --> 00:04:02,384
I was drawn here for the coffee too.

47
00:04:03,469 --> 00:04:04,678
I'm just saying.

48
00:04:15,189 --> 00:04:16,690
Are you free

49
00:04:18,108 --> 00:04:19,109
for lunch this Friday?

50
00:04:20,152 --> 00:04:21,320
<i>That's insane.</i>

51
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:26,366
How will you show your face
at work now? That's embarrassing.

52
00:04:27,701 --> 00:04:29,620
It's not even humiliating anymore.

53
00:04:30,037 --> 00:04:32,247
I guess
I can get used to humiliation.

54
00:04:32,956 --> 00:04:36,585
Friday lunch?

55
00:04:36,919 --> 00:04:38,587
Well...

56
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:41,006
I don't have any plans for lunch.

57
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,467
- What time?
- Around one.

58
00:04:44,009 --> 00:04:45,177
One should be fine.

59
00:04:47,012 --> 00:04:48,722
- Where?
- I will

60
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,641
not be the one choosing.

61
00:04:52,184 --> 00:04:53,185
Then me?

62
00:04:53,894 --> 00:04:55,813
What do you like to eat?

63
00:04:55,896 --> 00:04:57,648
JC will choose.

64
00:04:57,731 --> 00:05:01,026
They wanted to discuss something
and they want you to be there too.

65
00:05:02,027 --> 00:05:03,028
Is that okay with you?

66
00:05:04,321 --> 00:05:06,156
Yes, let's do that.

67
00:05:08,075 --> 00:05:09,326
<i>That's fine.</i>

68
00:05:09,868 --> 00:05:11,328
I bet he is

69
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:12,871
used to that.

70
00:05:13,872 --> 00:05:15,415
That's even worse.

71
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:20,587
The number of visitors
keeps going up.

72
00:05:20,879 --> 00:05:22,005
I need a screenshot.

73
00:05:23,882 --> 00:05:25,008
- You happy?
- Yes.

74
00:05:26,093 --> 00:05:27,594
To be honest, I was a bit worried.

75
00:05:27,678 --> 00:05:29,805
It's our first time
trying out a marketing project.

76
00:05:29,888 --> 00:05:32,140
I didn't expect it to do so well.

77
00:05:32,349 --> 00:05:34,643
You saw exactly
how important marketing was.

78
00:05:35,269 --> 00:05:37,145
Well, I admit that it went viral.

79
00:05:37,521 --> 00:05:39,982
Why don't we just scout Yeon-su?

80
00:05:40,190 --> 00:05:42,192
- What do you think?
- What are you saying?

81
00:05:42,276 --> 00:05:44,069
Why not? She knows what she's doing.

82
00:05:44,152 --> 00:05:45,487
She's friendly, witty

83
00:05:45,863 --> 00:05:47,489
and sometimes, she's cute.

84
00:05:48,866 --> 00:05:49,867
Cute?

85
00:05:50,534 --> 00:05:52,536
But then, she's not your type.

86
00:05:52,619 --> 00:05:54,371
You like assertive women.

87
00:05:54,997 --> 00:05:56,248
Gong Yeon-su is bold too.

88
00:05:58,917 --> 00:06:00,335
Yeon-su is bold?

89
00:06:05,799 --> 00:06:07,676
You're really bad at reading people

90
00:06:07,968 --> 00:06:09,344
especially women.

91
00:06:09,553 --> 00:06:11,221
You're only good at picking friends.

92
00:06:14,766 --> 00:06:17,603
I wonder what kind of man she likes.

93
00:06:20,564 --> 00:06:22,566
If she likes
thoughtful and sweet guys

94
00:06:22,649 --> 00:06:24,109
I'm the one.

95
00:06:25,861 --> 00:06:27,195
Jeez!

96
00:06:27,279 --> 00:06:29,031
Why won't they use their turn signal?

97
00:06:29,114 --> 00:06:30,407
Oh, jeez.

98
00:06:32,284 --> 00:06:37,205
MAKE ME TINGLE

99
00:06:37,289 --> 00:06:38,874
SEONGHYEON CIVIL SERVICE
PREPARATORY SCHOOL

100
00:06:38,957 --> 00:06:40,584
EPISODE 5

101
00:06:45,213 --> 00:06:46,423
I'm so tired.

102
00:06:46,506 --> 00:06:47,883
- Me too.
- Good job today.

103
00:06:47,966 --> 00:06:49,384
My knees are in pain.

104
00:06:49,468 --> 00:06:51,178
Me too. My back hurts too.

105
00:06:51,261 --> 00:06:52,262
Let's eat something at home.

106
00:06:52,346 --> 00:06:53,472
What do you want to eat?

107
00:06:53,555 --> 00:06:55,223
- I want fried chicken.
- Fried chicken?

108
00:06:55,307 --> 00:06:56,391
- Kang Si-eun.
- Later...

109
00:06:57,351 --> 00:06:58,477
- See you.
- Bye.

110
00:07:04,691 --> 00:07:06,443
What are you doing here?
You didn't tell me you were coming.

111
00:07:06,526 --> 00:07:08,028
How was I supposed to tell you

112
00:07:08,487 --> 00:07:09,780
when you wouldn't answer your phone?

113
00:07:11,365 --> 00:07:13,909
I was worried about you
because I couldn't reach you.

114
00:07:14,826 --> 00:07:15,827
I was busy.

115
00:07:16,578 --> 00:07:17,579
What's going on?

116
00:07:19,247 --> 00:07:20,791
What's suddenly gotten into you?

117
00:07:21,208 --> 00:07:22,334
Nam-su.

118
00:07:24,211 --> 00:07:25,212
We need to talk.

119
00:07:37,432 --> 00:07:39,142
Let's get married first.

120
00:07:39,226 --> 00:07:41,269
No, let me meet your family first.

121
00:07:41,353 --> 00:07:42,396
Then my family...

122
00:07:42,479 --> 00:07:44,523
I auditioned for Wonderbeat.

123
00:07:44,898 --> 00:07:46,191
And I made it.

124
00:07:48,944 --> 00:07:50,070
I'm joining them.

125
00:07:50,529 --> 00:07:51,530
That's my answer for you.

126
00:07:53,573 --> 00:07:55,742
- Si-eun.
- I'll call you soon.

127
00:07:55,826 --> 00:07:56,994
Come with me as my guardian.

128
00:08:02,290 --> 00:08:03,959
You can't just make a decision
on your own

129
00:08:04,042 --> 00:08:06,503
- without even talking to me.
- What if I did?

130
00:08:07,337 --> 00:08:08,463
Would that change anything?

131
00:08:08,714 --> 00:08:10,465
The decision is up to me anyway.

132
00:08:10,549 --> 00:08:12,801
It's not just about you.
It's about us.

133
00:08:14,469 --> 00:08:15,721
This is my life.

134
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,681
And it's my body.

135
00:08:20,642 --> 00:08:23,103
You know what I've gone through
to come this far.

136
00:08:23,186 --> 00:08:24,896
I've worked so hard for my dream.

137
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:26,314
Are you expecting me
to give up on that?

138
00:08:27,107 --> 00:08:28,358
I can.

139
00:08:28,442 --> 00:08:30,736
I can quit studying
and work in construction right now.

140
00:08:31,319 --> 00:08:32,654
For us, I...

141
00:08:33,530 --> 00:08:35,073
I can give up on my dream.

142
00:08:36,116 --> 00:08:37,409
You know why?

143
00:08:39,286 --> 00:08:41,038
Because that's not
what you really want to do.

144
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:44,624
You may have spent your whole life
without any goals for yourself

145
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,126
but I'm different.

146
00:08:47,711 --> 00:08:48,920
I don't want to live like that.

147
00:09:13,528 --> 00:09:14,571
Gong Yeon-su.

148
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:18,325
Seung-jun?

149
00:09:19,743 --> 00:09:20,911
Gosh.

150
00:09:22,162 --> 00:09:23,371
How have you been?

151
00:09:23,455 --> 00:09:25,332
Good.

152
00:09:25,791 --> 00:09:27,125
I've been well.

153
00:09:27,209 --> 00:09:29,169
- What about you?
- I've been well too.

154
00:09:32,422 --> 00:09:34,424
Anyway, what are you doing here?

155
00:09:34,508 --> 00:09:35,675
I'm meeting someone here.

156
00:09:35,759 --> 00:09:37,094
Are you?

157
00:09:37,427 --> 00:09:38,595
I'm meeting someone here too.

158
00:09:51,191 --> 00:09:54,820
By meeting someone, did you mean...

159
00:10:05,539 --> 00:10:07,916
- I'm the director, Jang Yu-jin.
- Nice to meet you.

160
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:09,960
And this is...

161
00:10:12,504 --> 00:10:14,506
I'm Choi Seung-jun from Marketing.

162
00:10:36,278 --> 00:10:38,613
I've gone over the proposal
you sent me.

163
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:40,574
I noticed the location
for the pop-up store is Busan.

164
00:10:40,657 --> 00:10:43,034
Our boss is from Busan.

165
00:10:43,118 --> 00:10:44,870
He has a stronger attachment to Busan
than to other cities.

166
00:10:44,953 --> 00:10:47,622
He also plans to expand
the chain business there later.

167
00:10:47,706 --> 00:10:51,084
Because he trusts her so much

168
00:10:51,543 --> 00:10:53,753
he put her in charge
of the entire chain business.

169
00:10:53,837 --> 00:10:55,797
Oh, I got it.

170
00:10:58,550 --> 00:10:59,634
Thank you.

171
00:11:03,096 --> 00:11:06,266
Anyway, from what I know

172
00:11:06,349 --> 00:11:10,187
you're not the type to be interested
in this field, Ms. Gong.

173
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:12,230
Haven't you mainly worked
on marketing for credit cards, banks

174
00:11:12,314 --> 00:11:15,775
and other brands
that have a more positive image?

175
00:11:21,656 --> 00:11:23,909
A good craftsman
never blames his tools.

176
00:11:24,284 --> 00:11:26,828
Because she's such
a competent marketer

177
00:11:26,912 --> 00:11:28,413
she doesn't limit herself
to any particular genre.

178
00:11:28,997 --> 00:11:30,832
She impressed me with the horizon

179
00:11:30,916 --> 00:11:32,375
and now she's hit it big
with the random box

180
00:11:32,459 --> 00:11:34,544
as soon as she joined my company.

181
00:11:34,628 --> 00:11:37,505
Was that her work?

182
00:11:37,589 --> 00:11:38,673
Yes.

183
00:11:39,174 --> 00:11:41,092
She's taught me that marketing isn't
about competing on products

184
00:11:41,176 --> 00:11:44,512
but about shaping perception.

185
00:11:59,861 --> 00:12:01,238
I didn't know

186
00:12:01,947 --> 00:12:04,449
you thought so highly of me.

187
00:12:05,367 --> 00:12:06,451
If you don't feel comfortable

188
00:12:06,534 --> 00:12:08,328
you don't have to come
to the meetings anymore.

189
00:12:08,662 --> 00:12:11,289
Mr. Yun or I can go instead.

190
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,960
Don't say that. I've got this.

191
00:12:15,835 --> 00:12:18,338
I'll make this project a success.

192
00:12:20,507 --> 00:12:21,508
There they are.

193
00:12:23,176 --> 00:12:24,928
I had a good time today.

194
00:12:25,136 --> 00:12:27,097
I look forward to working with you,
Ms. Gong.

195
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:28,473
Pleasure is mine.

196
00:12:28,890 --> 00:12:30,809
Mr. Dokgo,
can I have a minute with you?

197
00:12:31,059 --> 00:12:34,396
- Sure.
- Then I'll see you later.

198
00:12:35,605 --> 00:12:37,399
- I'll be waiting outside.
- Okay.

199
00:12:43,071 --> 00:12:44,698
Hey, is this about me?

200
00:12:45,073 --> 00:12:46,283
What?

201
00:12:46,366 --> 00:12:48,868
It's not like you
to take on this project.

202
00:12:48,952 --> 00:12:50,787
Is this about me?

203
00:12:51,454 --> 00:12:53,373
Or did you feel like
you needed a change in your life?

204
00:12:53,456 --> 00:12:55,959
- What's going on?
- What are you saying?

205
00:12:56,042 --> 00:12:58,461
Even so, he's not the one.

206
00:12:58,545 --> 00:13:00,005
You can tell just by looking at him
that something's off.

207
00:13:00,088 --> 00:13:01,423
Are you really that bad
at judging people?

208
00:13:01,506 --> 00:13:02,799
You're right.

209
00:13:02,882 --> 00:13:06,636
I was terrible at judging people

210
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:09,180
- wasn't I?
- Hey, I'm just worried about you...

211
00:13:10,348 --> 00:13:11,516
Leave me alone.

212
00:13:20,317 --> 00:13:23,194
Here is the list of products
for the Busan event.

213
00:13:23,278 --> 00:13:24,779
- Here you are.
- Thank you.

214
00:13:25,113 --> 00:13:28,491
I was thinking
about lube and condoms for samples.

215
00:13:28,575 --> 00:13:30,327
How about mini candles
instead of lube?

216
00:13:30,410 --> 00:13:31,870
We had a good response
to our candles.

217
00:13:31,953 --> 00:13:33,705
You want to give them away
as samples, not sell them?

218
00:13:34,664 --> 00:13:36,291
He's not cut out for business.

219
00:13:38,126 --> 00:13:39,878
Let's make it
a pop-up store exclusive.

220
00:13:39,961 --> 00:13:41,379
An exclusive?

221
00:13:42,213 --> 00:13:43,673
Think of the colors, images,
and scents

222
00:13:43,757 --> 00:13:45,633
that remind people of Busan.

223
00:13:45,884 --> 00:13:47,427
With the sea as our theme

224
00:13:47,510 --> 00:13:50,347
we'll revamp everything
from the packaging to the copy

225
00:13:50,847 --> 00:13:52,098
and create a random box in Busan.

226
00:13:53,141 --> 00:13:54,309
What do you think, boss?

227
00:13:55,643 --> 00:13:57,187
If it's a pop-up exclusive

228
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:59,189
we could draw in
our existing customers too.

229
00:13:59,272 --> 00:14:01,566
Yes, it's perfect. I love it.

230
00:14:03,401 --> 00:14:05,320
Min-hyung, make a reservation
at the candle workshop.

231
00:14:05,403 --> 00:14:06,404
Okay.

232
00:14:11,326 --> 00:14:13,745
There's a really good
<i>samgyetang </i>place nearby.

233
00:14:13,828 --> 00:14:15,080
Really? Have you been there?

234
00:14:15,205 --> 00:14:17,999
Of course. It's a hidden date course.

235
00:14:18,333 --> 00:14:20,627
- Really?
- After having <i>samgyetang </i>there

236
00:14:20,710 --> 00:14:22,337
there's a cafe nearby
that has an awesome chai latte.

237
00:14:22,420 --> 00:14:24,005
After that, there is...

238
00:14:24,089 --> 00:14:25,298
The end of the meeting.

239
00:14:25,799 --> 00:14:27,258
Good work.

240
00:14:41,272 --> 00:14:43,900
<i>A 200-year-old traditional soy sauce</i>
<i>for sale.</i>

241
00:14:43,983 --> 00:14:45,527
POST

242
00:15:05,630 --> 00:15:07,048
<i>You know why?</i>

243
00:15:08,091 --> 00:15:10,135
<i>Because that's not</i>
<i>what you really want to do.</i>

244
00:15:13,430 --> 00:15:14,764
<i>What do you mean?</i>

245
00:15:18,852 --> 00:15:20,562
I want to stop studying

246
00:15:21,312 --> 00:15:22,397
and start

247
00:15:23,606 --> 00:15:24,983
making money.

248
00:15:35,952 --> 00:15:37,370
The soup is too salty today.

249
00:15:38,079 --> 00:15:40,540
Maybe I boiled it for too long.

250
00:15:40,623 --> 00:15:42,584
- Should I make it again?
- Forget it.

251
00:15:51,301 --> 00:15:52,886
Are these lotus roots?

252
00:15:56,347 --> 00:15:57,432
<i>Sungnyung.</i>

253
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:13,323
You can make money

254
00:16:14,115 --> 00:16:17,035
after you pass the exam
and become a civil servant.

255
00:16:31,007 --> 00:16:32,383
Thank you for the meal.

256
00:16:40,141 --> 00:16:42,101
My goodness.

257
00:16:42,977 --> 00:16:44,938
- I'll go check on him.
- Yes.

258
00:16:45,021 --> 00:16:46,397
- Thank you for the meal.
- Yes.

259
00:16:53,655 --> 00:16:55,156
PASS THE CIVIL SERVICE EXAM
WITH EDUPANG FREE PASS

260
00:17:11,965 --> 00:17:13,216
For two.

261
00:17:24,811 --> 00:17:26,271
Aren't you on your way
to preparatory school?

262
00:17:27,522 --> 00:17:28,523
I am.

263
00:17:29,524 --> 00:17:31,109
But the bus takes too long.

264
00:17:31,192 --> 00:17:32,986
Exactly. That's why I'm taking it.

265
00:17:33,778 --> 00:17:35,363
After preparatory school,
I go to a study room.

266
00:17:35,446 --> 00:17:36,656
By the time I get home,
it's already too late.

267
00:17:37,740 --> 00:17:39,158
If not now,
I won't get to see the sun at all.

268
00:17:40,326 --> 00:17:42,495
Is that why
you dropped the bomb there?

269
00:17:43,162 --> 00:17:44,455
So you can see the sun from now on?

270
00:17:45,915 --> 00:17:48,126
If you were going to do it,
you might as well have done it right.

271
00:17:48,209 --> 00:17:49,711
You only ended up
shooting yourself in the foot.

272
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:51,838
Because I've never done it before.

273
00:17:52,297 --> 00:17:53,423
Must be nice for you.

274
00:17:53,965 --> 00:17:55,383
You get to do everything you want.

275
00:17:55,842 --> 00:17:58,219
- Me?
- It was your dream to be a marketer.

276
00:18:00,138 --> 00:18:01,889
It was something I wanted to do

277
00:18:02,473 --> 00:18:04,475
- but it wasn't my dream.
- What's the difference?

278
00:18:05,310 --> 00:18:06,686
They're different.

279
00:18:06,769 --> 00:18:09,689
What I want to do is
just for my own satisfaction

280
00:18:10,064 --> 00:18:11,316
but calling it a dream

281
00:18:11,774 --> 00:18:14,527
makes it sound
like my whole life depends on it.

282
00:18:15,236 --> 00:18:17,947
I didn't risk my life
on becoming a marketer.

283
00:18:18,031 --> 00:18:19,115
Then

284
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:21,075
what's the dream
you'd bet your life on?

285
00:18:25,455 --> 00:18:26,706
That's none of your business.

286
00:18:31,085 --> 00:18:32,211
I'm not sure

287
00:18:33,504 --> 00:18:34,714
what I want to do

288
00:18:35,173 --> 00:18:36,382
or if I even have a dream.

289
00:18:37,717 --> 00:18:38,926
My life is

290
00:18:40,261 --> 00:18:41,346
like a bus.

291
00:18:42,847 --> 00:18:44,515
It keeps going in circles.

292
00:18:45,350 --> 00:18:47,352
I can't even get off
unless it's at a designated stop.

293
00:18:51,773 --> 00:18:53,941
Would things have been different
if Dad were still alive?

294
00:18:58,946 --> 00:19:01,991
<i>This stop is Pureunsan Library.</i>

295
00:19:02,659 --> 00:19:06,120
<i>The next stop is</i>
<i>Jongno Station Exit One.</i>

296
00:19:09,791 --> 00:19:11,334
- Here.
- What's this?

297
00:19:11,709 --> 00:19:13,336
Take it. This is my stop.

298
00:19:16,589 --> 00:19:20,218
Dad would've given you money
in secret.

299
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:26,099
Make sure not to skip your meals.

300
00:19:47,787 --> 00:19:49,455
OUT OF ORDER

301
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:55,753
<i>See you at work by 10 a.m.</i>

302
00:21:06,032 --> 00:21:08,701
ELEVATOR SERVICE WILL BE UNAVAILABLE
DUE TO AN ELECTRICAL SUPPLY ISSUE

303
00:21:08,785 --> 00:21:09,994
- Excuse me.
- Hi.

304
00:21:10,369 --> 00:21:12,538
The lights are off in the stairwell.

305
00:21:12,622 --> 00:21:15,166
It looks like the power's out
in the whole line from Building 201.

306
00:21:16,292 --> 00:21:17,585
I don't know what's wrong with it.

307
00:21:17,668 --> 00:21:19,295
Will it be fixed by today?

308
00:21:19,378 --> 00:21:22,048
I was told it'll be fixed
by 10 p.m. at the latest.

309
00:21:22,131 --> 00:21:23,216
Okay.

310
00:21:47,865 --> 00:21:50,117
To the candle workshop.
I'll pay you double.

311
00:21:50,201 --> 00:21:51,285
What are you doing?

312
00:21:51,369 --> 00:21:53,371
Are you coming with us today?

313
00:21:53,454 --> 00:21:55,540
I just got a call
from the candle workshop.

314
00:21:55,623 --> 00:21:57,625
The essence we ordered is
going to be delayed.

315
00:21:57,708 --> 00:21:59,585
Is that so?
Should we leave a little later?

316
00:21:59,669 --> 00:22:02,380
I figured it might happen, so I made
a reservation at a <i>samgyetang </i>place.

317
00:22:02,672 --> 00:22:04,590
That place is awesome.

318
00:22:05,007 --> 00:22:07,426
All right. Let's go, Mr. Dokgo.
Hit the road.

319
00:22:13,516 --> 00:22:15,017
Can I put some music on?

320
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:17,645
I prefer to drive in silence.

321
00:22:22,441 --> 00:22:23,442
Put this on. Let's listen together.

322
00:22:25,278 --> 00:22:26,279
Thank you.

323
00:22:33,995 --> 00:22:35,580
- Wait. Is this...
- You know this song?

324
00:22:35,663 --> 00:22:38,499
Of course. It's my favorite song.

325
00:22:38,583 --> 00:22:41,377
At first, I thought
the title wasn't <i>Nagging</i>

326
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:42,628
but Henpecking.

327
00:22:50,052 --> 00:22:51,304
Here it comes.

328
00:22:51,387 --> 00:22:52,388
- Two, three.
- Two, three.

329
00:22:52,471 --> 00:22:56,475
<i>- I'm saying this for you</i>
<i>- I'm saying this for you</i>

330
00:22:56,559 --> 00:22:58,811
<i>- It's only nagging</i>
<i>- It's only nagging</i>

331
00:22:58,895 --> 00:23:00,521
<i>- When you don't listen</i>
<i>- When you don't listen</i>

332
00:23:00,605 --> 00:23:04,901
<i>- Let's stop</i>
<i>- Let's stop</i>

333
00:23:04,984 --> 00:23:07,820
<i>- We don't even have enough time</i>
<i>- We don't even have enough time</i>

334
00:23:25,713 --> 00:23:28,299
Mr. Yun, you have good taste.

335
00:23:28,382 --> 00:23:29,508
Of course.

336
00:23:30,176 --> 00:23:32,428
This song has to be sung in a duet,
you know what I mean?

337
00:23:32,511 --> 00:23:35,389
Of course. Let's sing it together
in the next team dinner.

338
00:23:35,765 --> 00:23:36,891
Sounds good.

339
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:39,060
Seriously, let's stop.

340
00:23:43,147 --> 00:23:44,273
Enjoy.

341
00:23:44,649 --> 00:23:46,400
This is lacquer tree <i>baeksuk</i>.

342
00:23:46,484 --> 00:23:48,069
Do you like drumsticks?

343
00:23:48,152 --> 00:23:49,487
I like lean meat.

344
00:23:49,862 --> 00:23:50,988
I prefer drumsticks.

345
00:23:52,323 --> 00:23:53,532
Have you heard

346
00:23:53,908 --> 00:23:56,410
- of the White-Yolk Fatalism?
- What's that?

347
00:23:57,578 --> 00:24:01,123
People who prefer different parts
of an egg are meant to be together.

348
00:24:01,207 --> 00:24:03,167
Because you like different parts

349
00:24:03,250 --> 00:24:04,710
you have nothing to fight over.

350
00:24:07,421 --> 00:24:09,090
Actually, I just made that up.

351
00:24:09,298 --> 00:24:10,466
But it makes sense, right?

352
00:24:12,802 --> 00:24:14,220
You're right.

353
00:24:16,764 --> 00:24:18,474
That's about taste, not fate.

354
00:24:19,308 --> 00:24:21,644
You talk about taste a lot

355
00:24:21,727 --> 00:24:23,312
Mr. Dokgo.

356
00:24:23,396 --> 00:24:26,691
People with picky tastes
always talk about tastes.

357
00:24:26,774 --> 00:24:30,236
Then what is your taste, Mr. Dokgo?

358
00:24:30,528 --> 00:24:34,115
Have you ever met someone
who was a perfect fit for you?

359
00:24:34,198 --> 00:24:36,867
You mean personality or sex?

360
00:24:36,951 --> 00:24:38,202
That's not what she's talking about.

361
00:24:38,285 --> 00:24:40,997
She's asking if you've ever been
in a relationship before.

362
00:24:41,288 --> 00:24:43,416
Well, if you count
a one-day encounter too...

363
00:24:43,499 --> 00:24:45,584
A one-night stand isn't
a relationship.

364
00:24:45,668 --> 00:24:46,752
Strictly speaking, that is.

365
00:24:47,545 --> 00:24:49,505
Everyone has different standards.

366
00:24:49,588 --> 00:24:52,883
The essence of a relationship lies
not in the moment but consistency.

367
00:24:52,967 --> 00:24:54,885
It's built
on consistent interest, feelings

368
00:24:54,969 --> 00:24:56,012
and a sense of responsibility.

369
00:24:56,095 --> 00:24:59,473
Relationship, date, sex,
and marriage.

370
00:24:59,724 --> 00:25:02,143
You really seem to enjoy
defining everything, don't you?

371
00:25:02,226 --> 00:25:04,854
They're all major factors

372
00:25:04,937 --> 00:25:06,439
that determine
the important matters in life.

373
00:25:06,522 --> 00:25:08,607
It's only normal
to examine them carefully

374
00:25:08,691 --> 00:25:09,900
and think things through.

375
00:25:11,777 --> 00:25:13,237
How could a one-day encounter

376
00:25:13,779 --> 00:25:16,365
possibly be the start
of a relationship?

377
00:25:18,451 --> 00:25:20,036
What are you,
the head of the royal court?

378
00:25:22,371 --> 00:25:24,832
Sometimes, a one-day encounter

379
00:25:24,915 --> 00:25:27,001
does become the start
of a relationship.

380
00:25:29,670 --> 00:25:33,049
Like how one good kiss leads
to asking someone out on a date.

381
00:25:39,138 --> 00:25:41,766
Okay, that's enough. Let's eat now.

382
00:25:41,849 --> 00:25:42,975
The food is getting cold.

383
00:25:43,059 --> 00:25:44,643
Enjoy the lean meat.

384
00:25:54,236 --> 00:25:55,362
No matter how I think about it

385
00:25:55,738 --> 00:25:57,656
I don't think you've ever been
in a relationship before.

386
00:25:58,574 --> 00:25:59,909
What are you talking about? Me?

387
00:26:00,451 --> 00:26:03,537
You've never liked anyone
or loved anyone

388
00:26:03,621 --> 00:26:05,623
emotionally or mentally.

389
00:26:06,332 --> 00:26:08,918
Because you've never done it before,
you think love is an illusion.

390
00:26:09,001 --> 00:26:11,045
You're talking like
you've done it a lot.

391
00:26:11,128 --> 00:26:13,089
I may not have a lot of experience

392
00:26:13,172 --> 00:26:14,715
but I do believe in love

393
00:26:14,799 --> 00:26:16,092
unlike someone.

394
00:26:18,219 --> 00:26:22,098
Humans are emotional beings
as well as physical beings.

395
00:26:22,348 --> 00:26:24,683
At least,
I'm doing one of the two properly

396
00:26:24,767 --> 00:26:26,018
unlike someone.

397
00:26:26,727 --> 00:26:28,813
- You think it's funny?
- It's not boring.

398
00:26:43,661 --> 00:26:46,580
- Are you okay?
- You know what?

399
00:26:46,831 --> 00:26:47,957
I think something is wrong with me.

400
00:26:52,336 --> 00:26:53,671
Oh, no. I'll be fine.

401
00:26:53,754 --> 00:26:55,131
Don't worry about me.

402
00:26:55,214 --> 00:26:56,340
Are you sure you're going to be okay?

403
00:26:56,423 --> 00:26:57,883
I can reschedule the workshop.

404
00:26:59,593 --> 00:27:00,678
What is it?

405
00:27:01,345 --> 00:27:02,596
Never mind that.

406
00:27:02,680 --> 00:27:05,599
Do I look hideous right now?

407
00:27:05,683 --> 00:27:07,393
- Hideous.
- Just go!

408
00:27:08,769 --> 00:27:09,937
See you.

409
00:27:11,397 --> 00:27:13,649
Would it be okay
to let him go by himself?

410
00:27:14,191 --> 00:27:16,944
I gave the driver my number
just in case.

411
00:27:17,027 --> 00:27:18,195
Let's go back to work.

412
00:27:32,751 --> 00:27:35,129
CUSTOM CANDLE MAKING

413
00:27:59,904 --> 00:28:01,071
Mr. Dokgo?

414
00:28:06,994 --> 00:28:09,121
I've brought some options

415
00:28:09,205 --> 00:28:10,581
with the summer beach vibe
you wanted.

416
00:28:10,664 --> 00:28:13,834
Here we have
citrus, aqua, and floral scents.

417
00:28:21,342 --> 00:28:23,469
This has a bitter kick.

418
00:28:23,552 --> 00:28:24,762
But it's not lemon.

419
00:28:24,845 --> 00:28:27,139
- It's grapefruit.
- Oh, grapefruit.

420
00:28:27,223 --> 00:28:28,766
Take your time with them.

421
00:28:28,849 --> 00:28:30,100
- Okay.
- Thank you.

422
00:28:35,022 --> 00:28:36,357
The aqua scent leaves a nice trail.

423
00:28:36,815 --> 00:28:39,360
It's kind of floral
and kind of like green apple.

424
00:28:42,404 --> 00:28:44,698
Do you think he made it
to the hospital by now?

425
00:28:44,782 --> 00:28:45,991
I mean, Mr. Yun.

426
00:28:46,492 --> 00:28:48,953
Well, no news is good news.

427
00:28:49,036 --> 00:28:50,329
What time is it?

428
00:28:54,875 --> 00:28:56,961
Oh, no.

429
00:28:57,044 --> 00:28:59,797
That's undiluted.
The smell won't wash out easily.

430
00:29:25,739 --> 00:29:28,450
Don't worry.
It's not because of the smell.

431
00:29:29,535 --> 00:29:31,078
I see.

432
00:29:36,959 --> 00:29:38,919
<i>Ms. Gong, I'm feeling a lot better.</i>

433
00:29:39,545 --> 00:29:41,005
<i>My lips look awful, don't they?</i>

434
00:29:42,047 --> 00:29:44,258
<i>You totally have</i>
<i>Tom Hardy lips right now.</i>

435
00:29:44,508 --> 00:29:46,135
<i>Don't worry. It's sexy.</i>

436
00:29:48,178 --> 00:29:49,221
Who is it?

437
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:51,724
Oh, it's Mr. Yun.

438
00:29:51,807 --> 00:29:52,808
He says he's much better now.

439
00:29:53,392 --> 00:29:54,893
Why didn't he just text me...

440
00:29:54,977 --> 00:29:56,395
Anyway, that's a relief.

441
00:29:56,478 --> 00:29:58,314
It really gave me a scare.

442
00:29:58,397 --> 00:29:59,565
He's fine.

443
00:29:59,648 --> 00:30:02,192
He had the same reaction
while feeding a stray cat once.

444
00:30:03,944 --> 00:30:05,195
Plus, he's allergic to the sun.

445
00:30:07,698 --> 00:30:10,117
That guy is
a lot more fragile than I am.

446
00:30:10,326 --> 00:30:11,744
I see.

447
00:30:18,792 --> 00:30:19,793
Tom Hardy?

448
00:30:22,171 --> 00:30:25,132
She really has
the prettiest way with words.

449
00:30:40,898 --> 00:30:42,232
Aren't you going home?

450
00:30:46,570 --> 00:30:48,155
We've still got things to discuss.

451
00:30:48,238 --> 00:30:50,282
Let's finish up
over another cup of tea.

452
00:30:51,450 --> 00:30:52,451
Okay...

453
00:30:56,830 --> 00:30:59,625
I'm looking to divide
the pop-up space

454
00:30:59,708 --> 00:31:01,752
into experience, event,
and merchandise zones.

455
00:31:02,336 --> 00:31:04,630
But I'm worried
if there will be enough space.

456
00:31:04,713 --> 00:31:06,382
It should be more than enough.

457
00:31:06,799 --> 00:31:08,717
Have you thought
about the design concept?

458
00:31:08,801 --> 00:31:09,927
Oh, yes.

459
00:31:10,010 --> 00:31:12,846
I plan to run it by JC, though.

460
00:31:12,930 --> 00:31:14,640
We have to consider
the budget constraints.

461
00:31:15,641 --> 00:31:18,727
Does that mean
dealing with Mr. Choi Seung-jun?

462
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:21,355
Well...

463
00:31:22,022 --> 00:31:24,691
Naturally,
since he's the guy in charge.

464
00:31:30,531 --> 00:31:33,409
Do you have somewhere to be?

465
00:31:33,492 --> 00:31:35,411
You've been checking the time.

466
00:31:35,494 --> 00:31:36,578
Not really.

467
00:31:37,538 --> 00:31:39,998
The elevator is
under maintenance until 10 p.m.

468
00:31:40,749 --> 00:31:41,750
I see.

469
00:31:43,001 --> 00:31:46,088
You can just take the stairs.

470
00:32:09,153 --> 00:32:10,821
I'm all right, so get going.

471
00:32:10,904 --> 00:32:13,866
I only have to kill an hour or two.

472
00:32:14,741 --> 00:32:16,702
- Let's walk up.
- But it's pretty high.

473
00:32:16,952 --> 00:32:20,414
Come on.
I've got enough stamina for this.

474
00:32:29,089 --> 00:32:30,257
Keep up with me.

475
00:32:41,852 --> 00:32:44,104
Stairs are quite the workout.

476
00:32:44,605 --> 00:32:47,065
I've only ever lived
in a hanok house.

477
00:32:48,734 --> 00:32:49,860
That's why

478
00:32:50,277 --> 00:32:52,404
I'm good at hopping walls.

479
00:32:57,409 --> 00:33:01,580
But seriously,
you've never had a first love

480
00:33:02,039 --> 00:33:03,248
through all of school and college?

481
00:33:05,626 --> 00:33:06,752
When I was little

482
00:33:07,544 --> 00:33:09,296
even Man-su next door

483
00:33:09,379 --> 00:33:11,632
had a crush on Cho-rong
across the street.

484
00:33:12,591 --> 00:33:13,842
Who's Man-su?

485
00:33:14,468 --> 00:33:16,428
A poodle. He was absolutely cute.

486
00:33:18,972 --> 00:33:20,015
16TH FLOOR
15TH FLOOR

487
00:33:25,896 --> 00:33:27,314
20TH FLOOR
19TH FLOOR

488
00:33:29,483 --> 00:33:32,736
Why do you live up so high anyway?

489
00:33:33,487 --> 00:33:34,738
This is basically

490
00:33:35,030 --> 00:33:37,324
a modern-day Rapunzel situation.

491
00:33:39,868 --> 00:33:41,036
This way.

492
00:33:43,997 --> 00:33:46,875
Wait. Hold up.

493
00:33:49,044 --> 00:33:50,087
Take a deep breath.

494
00:33:50,712 --> 00:33:52,214
We only have two floors left.

495
00:33:54,091 --> 00:33:55,259
Two more...

496
00:34:11,483 --> 00:34:12,609
What's wrong?

497
00:34:13,110 --> 00:34:15,571
- Is your back acting up again?
- My back...

498
00:34:18,574 --> 00:34:19,575
Hop on my back.

499
00:34:22,077 --> 00:34:23,704
No, I'm fine.

500
00:34:23,787 --> 00:34:26,456
Want to walk down 20 floors alone?
Or go up 2 more with me?

501
00:34:26,540 --> 00:34:27,874
Twenty floors?

502
00:34:30,919 --> 00:34:31,920
I can

503
00:34:33,213 --> 00:34:34,339
do it myself.

504
00:34:40,012 --> 00:34:41,722
Come on. Get on my back.

505
00:34:46,268 --> 00:34:48,270
- Here, grab this.
- What...

506
00:34:50,606 --> 00:34:51,982
Don't tense up. It makes you heavier.

507
00:34:53,442 --> 00:35:01,450
I'm sorry.

508
00:35:39,446 --> 00:35:40,447
Oh, my.

509
00:35:43,283 --> 00:35:45,077
Drink this.
I'll go wash up real quick.

510
00:35:45,410 --> 00:35:46,411
Excuse me?

511
00:35:50,332 --> 00:35:51,416
- Okay.
- Good.

512
00:36:17,484 --> 00:36:20,112
- Hey, are you feeling okay?
- Totally.

513
00:36:20,195 --> 00:36:22,864
Whoever invented antihistamines
deserves a Nobel Prize.

514
00:36:22,948 --> 00:36:23,949
I'm pretty sure they did.

515
00:36:24,950 --> 00:36:27,452
I'm almost at your door
with some fried chicken.

516
00:36:27,536 --> 00:36:30,163
Dude, you had an allergic reaction
to sumac chicken. Why bring more?

517
00:36:30,247 --> 00:36:32,874
<i>Don't blame the chicken.</i>
<i>It's the sumac's fault.</i>

518
00:36:32,958 --> 00:36:35,085
<i>- You got any beer at your place?</i>
- Don't come.

519
00:36:35,168 --> 00:36:36,670
- I'm tired. I'm hanging up.
- What?

520
00:36:36,753 --> 00:36:38,171
Why not? I'm already...

521
00:37:01,820 --> 00:37:03,572
Is he done?

522
00:37:08,118 --> 00:37:09,661
<i>What's wrong with me?</i>

523
00:37:12,497 --> 00:37:14,416
Oh, wait.

524
00:37:20,756 --> 00:37:22,299
My back's fine now.

525
00:37:31,057 --> 00:37:32,267
Where are you going?

526
00:37:41,735 --> 00:37:42,903
How's your back?

527
00:37:44,237 --> 00:37:45,697
It's fine now.

528
00:37:45,822 --> 00:37:48,074
- So, I'm...
- You're leaving?

529
00:37:51,787 --> 00:37:53,163
I'm a little hurt.

530
00:37:53,705 --> 00:37:54,790
Excuse me?

531
00:37:56,541 --> 00:37:57,751
Do you want to wash up?

532
00:37:59,336 --> 00:38:00,420
Now?

533
00:38:00,712 --> 00:38:01,922
Here?

534
00:38:06,134 --> 00:38:07,469
Right here, right now.

535
00:38:21,942 --> 00:38:23,193
No.

536
00:38:24,611 --> 00:38:26,613
I really shouldn't.

537
00:38:27,364 --> 00:38:28,365
No.

538
00:38:29,366 --> 00:38:31,701
Ms. Gong?

539
00:38:35,413 --> 00:38:36,665
Did you fall asleep?

540
00:38:44,464 --> 00:38:46,299
- A bit higher.
- Here?

541
00:38:46,383 --> 00:38:48,677
Yes, but a bit to the right.

542
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:49,928
Here, right?

543
00:38:50,220 --> 00:38:52,097
Yes, right there.

544
00:38:55,642 --> 00:38:56,768
There we go.

545
00:38:58,228 --> 00:39:00,355
Thank you.

546
00:39:00,814 --> 00:39:02,774
So how long has your back
been bothering you?

547
00:39:04,693 --> 00:39:06,987
It's been a while.

548
00:39:09,739 --> 00:39:11,783
Believe it or not, my family

549
00:39:11,867 --> 00:39:14,286
holds 22 memorial services a year.

550
00:39:15,453 --> 00:39:19,040
When I was little, my dad used
to sneak behind my grandpa's back

551
00:39:19,124 --> 00:39:23,044
to help my mom with the <i>jeon</i>
and all the prep.

552
00:39:24,421 --> 00:39:28,550
But after he passed away,
I took over.

553
00:39:29,175 --> 00:39:31,845
And eventually,
it took a toll on my back.

554
00:39:37,517 --> 00:39:38,560
Gosh.

555
00:39:39,102 --> 00:39:43,064
My dad made
the best shiitake mushroom <i>jeon</i>.

556
00:39:44,441 --> 00:39:47,777
You usually carve
a little star on the cap, right?

557
00:39:47,861 --> 00:39:50,238
He'd always make one into a heart

558
00:39:50,322 --> 00:39:53,742
and save it just for me.

559
00:39:58,455 --> 00:39:59,664
Sometimes...

560
00:40:01,207 --> 00:40:02,751
I miss that so much.

561
00:40:08,715 --> 00:40:10,967
Sounds like
you two were really close.

562
00:40:12,636 --> 00:40:13,678
Yes.

563
00:40:14,471 --> 00:40:16,348
Very close.

564
00:40:23,438 --> 00:40:24,898
Anyway, I wonder why

565
00:40:26,399 --> 00:40:30,779
I'm telling you all this
while lying flat on my stomach here.

566
00:40:33,531 --> 00:40:34,699
Tell me about it.

567
00:40:35,367 --> 00:40:37,410
Why did I have to spill that liquid

568
00:40:38,203 --> 00:40:40,538
and drag you into this mess?

569
00:40:42,415 --> 00:40:44,501
Today really was a disaster
from start to finish.

570
00:40:48,004 --> 00:40:51,007
I suppose it wasn't

571
00:40:51,174 --> 00:40:52,926
entirely a disaster.

572
00:41:02,268 --> 00:41:05,271
I actually enjoyed today.

573
00:41:05,939 --> 00:41:07,691
We had good food

574
00:41:08,024 --> 00:41:10,276
got some coffee,
and walked in the park.

575
00:41:12,320 --> 00:41:15,448
We even got a stair workout in
at the end.

576
00:41:18,243 --> 00:41:21,246
We can grab a meal,
have coffee, and take a walk.

577
00:41:21,913 --> 00:41:24,290
That's my idea of a date.

578
00:41:25,959 --> 00:41:27,085
You think?

579
00:41:27,168 --> 00:41:28,378
You know...

580
00:41:29,129 --> 00:41:33,508
when I asked you out on a date

581
00:41:33,591 --> 00:41:37,762
it wasn't just because of the kiss.

582
00:41:38,888 --> 00:41:41,016
I had this feeling
that going on a date with you

583
00:41:41,224 --> 00:41:43,184
would help me

584
00:41:44,436 --> 00:41:46,229
venture down new paths

585
00:41:47,230 --> 00:41:49,149
and finally break out of my shell.

586
00:41:54,487 --> 00:41:55,697
If that's the case...

587
00:41:57,699 --> 00:41:59,743
are you open
to trying my kind of date too?

588
00:42:00,910 --> 00:42:03,246
- Sorry?
- Since we did

589
00:42:03,329 --> 00:42:05,040
your idea of a date today

590
00:42:06,416 --> 00:42:08,918
maybe we could give mine a shot.

591
00:42:10,003 --> 00:42:12,047
So you want to sleep with me?

592
00:42:12,422 --> 00:42:14,466
To me, that's a date.

593
00:42:28,229 --> 00:42:30,190
When I say dance, you say...

594
00:42:31,191 --> 00:42:33,193
Goodness. Ms. Gong?

595
00:42:34,235 --> 00:42:36,780
I must go home.

596
00:42:50,794 --> 00:42:53,129
<i>Speed bump ahead.</i>

597
00:42:56,466 --> 00:42:58,176
You should've rested a bit longer.

598
00:42:59,260 --> 00:43:00,595
Are you sure you don't need
to go to the ER?

599
00:43:02,222 --> 00:43:04,182
- Just home...
- Okay, home.

600
00:43:07,185 --> 00:43:08,436
Ms. Gong.

601
00:43:08,520 --> 00:43:10,897
Do you think eating this
will take your mind off the pain?

602
00:43:17,737 --> 00:43:18,780
I'm sorry

603
00:43:19,572 --> 00:43:22,867
but could you take it easy
on the speed bumps?

604
00:43:23,118 --> 00:43:25,036
Hey, watch the speed bumps.

605
00:43:25,120 --> 00:43:26,371
Oh, here it comes.

606
00:43:26,454 --> 00:43:27,497
Bump!

607
00:43:34,879 --> 00:43:36,047
Good job.

608
00:43:44,722 --> 00:43:47,934
HANOK VILLAGE ENTRANCE

609
00:43:49,811 --> 00:43:52,313
I can really manage on my own.

610
00:43:52,689 --> 00:43:54,524
Come on. We'll walk you home.

611
00:43:56,943 --> 00:43:59,821
I can take it from here.

612
00:44:00,655 --> 00:44:02,031
I'm really okay.

613
00:44:09,622 --> 00:44:10,999
I don't think you can.

614
00:44:11,875 --> 00:44:13,418
I'm sorry.

615
00:44:14,002 --> 00:44:15,461
Could one of you...

616
00:44:23,011 --> 00:44:26,514
Please help me to the door.

617
00:44:26,598 --> 00:44:29,225
Of course. I'll be right back.

618
00:44:29,517 --> 00:44:30,602
What?

619
00:44:31,352 --> 00:44:33,062
- Oh, okay.
- Hand me your bag.

620
00:44:33,813 --> 00:44:35,273
Thank you.

621
00:44:41,154 --> 00:44:42,363
I'm so sorry.

622
00:44:43,489 --> 00:44:44,866
There's no need to apologize.

623
00:44:53,458 --> 00:44:55,376
So how exactly
do you know our Yeon-su?

624
00:44:57,795 --> 00:45:00,256
We're just work colleagues.

625
00:45:00,924 --> 00:45:03,134
Yes, we work at the same company.

626
00:45:03,218 --> 00:45:06,179
You've got such kind and round eyes.

627
00:45:06,679 --> 00:45:08,306
I can tell you're warm-hearted.

628
00:45:10,808 --> 00:45:13,228
- Oh, let me. I'll do it.
- Thank you.

629
00:45:17,273 --> 00:45:18,691
No, you...

630
00:45:27,742 --> 00:45:28,868
Close the doors.

631
00:45:32,914 --> 00:45:35,291
Mr. Yun, what's your family clan?

632
00:45:35,375 --> 00:45:37,669
I'm the 31st-generation descendant
of the Unjeong Yun clan.

633
00:45:37,752 --> 00:45:39,045
Unjeong, I see.

634
00:45:39,545 --> 00:45:41,547
Isn't that located in Gojin?

635
00:45:41,631 --> 00:45:43,258
- Oh, come on.
- That's right, sir.

636
00:45:43,341 --> 00:45:45,176
And your family?

637
00:45:45,426 --> 00:45:47,011
I have my parents
and three older sisters.

638
00:45:47,095 --> 00:45:49,264
I'm the youngest and the only son.

639
00:45:49,347 --> 00:45:51,349
You have quite a full house.

640
00:45:52,850 --> 00:45:54,477
Do you perform ancestral rites?

641
00:45:54,560 --> 00:45:57,063
The eldest uncle's family
handles the ancestral rites.

642
00:45:58,982 --> 00:46:00,733
As it should be.

643
00:46:04,737 --> 00:46:07,573
- They say filial piety
- It's scary.

644
00:46:07,657 --> 00:46:09,450
and gratitude to your ancestors

645
00:46:09,534 --> 00:46:11,577
are what bring good fortune
to a household.

646
00:46:12,036 --> 00:46:13,454
There are
way too many people these days

647
00:46:13,538 --> 00:46:15,957
who have no respect for their roots.

648
00:46:36,436 --> 00:46:37,520
Dal?

649
00:46:50,783 --> 00:46:53,161
Should I make a call
so he can hurry back out?

650
00:46:54,078 --> 00:46:55,163
It's fine.

651
00:46:55,621 --> 00:46:56,622
He'll be here eventually.

652
00:47:02,378 --> 00:47:04,005
Do you usually come home around now
after classes?

653
00:47:04,714 --> 00:47:05,923
I actually skipped my classes today.

654
00:47:07,216 --> 00:47:08,217
I'm thinking

655
00:47:09,135 --> 00:47:10,595
of quitting my studies.

656
00:47:12,638 --> 00:47:14,432
You're not going
to marry my sister, are you?

657
00:47:16,684 --> 00:47:18,144
That's why you lied.

658
00:47:21,272 --> 00:47:22,732
I know you don't have azoospermia.

659
00:47:23,691 --> 00:47:25,276
Since your secret's out

660
00:47:25,735 --> 00:47:27,278
should I spill one of mine?

661
00:47:28,112 --> 00:47:29,781
No, that's not necessary.

662
00:47:29,864 --> 00:47:30,948
My girlfriend...

663
00:47:33,242 --> 00:47:34,243
is pregnant.

664
00:47:38,081 --> 00:47:40,291
That's something to celebrate, right?

665
00:47:41,209 --> 00:47:42,585
She doesn't want to keep it.

666
00:47:42,668 --> 00:47:44,587
She says she can't give up
on her dreams.

667
00:47:45,088 --> 00:47:46,214
And I get it.

668
00:47:47,215 --> 00:47:48,758
Dancing is her whole life.

669
00:47:49,050 --> 00:47:50,968
Oh, she's a dancer.

670
00:47:56,891 --> 00:47:58,726
I first saw her through the window
of her studio.

671
00:48:07,068 --> 00:48:08,778
<i>She was drenched in sweat</i>

672
00:48:09,612 --> 00:48:12,031
<i>looking so happy while dancing.</i>

673
00:48:13,866 --> 00:48:15,159
It was mesmerizing.

674
00:48:17,995 --> 00:48:20,706
I realized
she had something I was missing.

675
00:48:21,499 --> 00:48:23,334
It was that exact passion I fell for.

676
00:48:25,002 --> 00:48:26,879
It'd be too selfish of me
to crush that, wouldn't it?

677
00:48:30,049 --> 00:48:31,300
The truth is...

678
00:48:33,386 --> 00:48:34,929
I want to take responsibility.

679
00:48:35,263 --> 00:48:37,098
Why are you telling me all this?

680
00:48:38,808 --> 00:48:40,309
Because I don't have
another guy to talk to.

681
00:48:42,395 --> 00:48:44,439
I don't have anyone
to give me advice man-to-man

682
00:48:44,522 --> 00:48:47,483
even if it means cursing me out
or cheering me on.

683
00:48:48,943 --> 00:48:50,361
But I felt like
you'd at least listen.

684
00:48:51,279 --> 00:48:52,613
If my dad were still around

685
00:48:53,531 --> 00:48:55,241
he'd obviously beat me half to death.

686
00:49:01,914 --> 00:49:03,791
I truly don't know what to do.

687
00:49:04,333 --> 00:49:07,587
There's only one thing
you can and should do.

688
00:49:11,757 --> 00:49:12,967
Respect her.

689
00:49:13,050 --> 00:49:15,052
Whatever she decides

690
00:49:15,761 --> 00:49:17,346
respect her decision

691
00:49:17,430 --> 00:49:18,848
and support her.

692
00:49:19,807 --> 00:49:21,767
That's how you take responsibility.

693
00:49:32,528 --> 00:49:34,322
<i>Responsibility isn't</i>
<i>that complicated.</i>

694
00:49:34,405 --> 00:49:36,073
For a man, there's nothing
more important

695
00:49:36,157 --> 00:49:37,867
than devotion to his family.

696
00:49:37,950 --> 00:49:41,370
The basics are always
the hardest, yet the most honorable.

697
00:49:41,454 --> 00:49:43,456
Exactly!

698
00:49:45,166 --> 00:49:46,292
Oh, goodness.

699
00:49:51,422 --> 00:49:54,050
Do you have any intentions
of getting married?

700
00:49:56,427 --> 00:50:00,640
Grandpa, why would you ask him that?

701
00:50:05,561 --> 00:50:07,605
What... No, wait.

702
00:50:09,273 --> 00:50:10,691
- Aunt.
- Absolutely.

703
00:50:10,775 --> 00:50:12,735
The world might be changing

704
00:50:12,860 --> 00:50:14,820
but I still believe
everyone needs a life partner.

705
00:50:14,904 --> 00:50:15,947
Indeed.

706
00:50:16,030 --> 00:50:18,282
Building a life
with the person you love...

707
00:50:18,699 --> 00:50:22,036
Isn't that the true happiness
and calling of a human being?

708
00:50:22,119 --> 00:50:23,412
Precisely!

709
00:50:26,082 --> 00:50:28,668
A harmonious marriage
and a peaceful home are

710
00:50:28,751 --> 00:50:30,294
what guarantee success
in the outside world.

711
00:50:30,378 --> 00:50:32,380
You're right. Peace at home
brings success to everything.

712
00:50:32,463 --> 00:50:33,714
Peace at home?

713
00:50:36,592 --> 00:50:38,094
My goodness.

714
00:50:39,512 --> 00:50:42,682
Get home safely. Let's grab
some <i>makgeolli </i>next time you visit.

715
00:50:42,765 --> 00:50:43,808
I'd love that.

716
00:50:44,350 --> 00:50:47,853
Baek-hee, let's cook up
another chicken sometime soon.

717
00:50:47,937 --> 00:50:49,021
Yes, Mother.

718
00:50:50,898 --> 00:50:52,483
- I'm home.
- Welcome back.

719
00:50:55,236 --> 00:50:56,487
Traitor.

720
00:50:58,656 --> 00:51:00,157
What is he saying?

721
00:51:04,662 --> 00:51:06,455
I told you to go inside.

722
00:51:06,539 --> 00:51:07,957
You're so stubborn.

723
00:51:08,040 --> 00:51:10,001
I'm okay. It's a lot better.

724
00:51:10,501 --> 00:51:12,962
Are you okay too?

725
00:51:13,045 --> 00:51:14,255
Absolutely.

726
00:51:14,338 --> 00:51:16,424
One injection
and the swelling went right down.

727
00:51:19,010 --> 00:51:20,845
I'm sorry about today.

728
00:51:20,928 --> 00:51:22,888
My grandpa
really caught us off guard.

729
00:51:22,972 --> 00:51:24,640
There's no need to be sorry.

730
00:51:25,600 --> 00:51:27,184
I actually had a great time.

731
00:51:27,268 --> 00:51:30,354
I got to drink dandelion tea
and tour a traditional home.

732
00:51:31,647 --> 00:51:32,982
It was fun.

733
00:51:34,150 --> 00:51:36,652
I've always had a way
of charming the elders, you see.

734
00:51:37,903 --> 00:51:41,657
That explains why my grandpa
wouldn't stop talking.

735
00:51:41,741 --> 00:51:43,826
I think he was
completely won over by me.

736
00:51:43,909 --> 00:51:48,080
Exactly. Why did you have to give
such textbook-perfect answers?

737
00:51:48,164 --> 00:51:49,415
That's just who I am.

738
00:51:56,088 --> 00:51:57,214
Ms. Gong.

739
00:51:58,174 --> 00:51:59,800
Do you have any plans
for next weekend?

740
00:52:00,926 --> 00:52:03,471
- Next weekend?
- If you're free

741
00:52:04,305 --> 00:52:05,681
would you go on a date with me?

742
00:52:07,767 --> 00:52:09,226
We can grab a meal

743
00:52:09,810 --> 00:52:12,438
have tea, and take a walk.

744
00:52:14,899 --> 00:52:15,983
What do you say?

745
00:52:18,444 --> 00:52:20,112
I'd like to get to know you.

746
00:53:00,945 --> 00:53:03,072
If you need time to think...

747
00:53:04,657 --> 00:53:05,658
Let's do it.

748
00:53:10,871 --> 00:53:12,707
Let's go on a date.

749
00:53:19,672 --> 00:53:22,758
MAKE ME TINGLE

750
00:54:59,271 --> 00:55:01,232
Subtitles by Songmi You
and Eunjin Erica Kim
